>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SElim`

``` hol4
clasetLib.SElim : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a safe elimination rule for one tactic invocation.

`SElim th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a classical-rule
marker. A tactic consuming it adds `th` to a temporary rule set as a safe
elimination rule. An elimination rule uses its major premise to match an
assumption and its conclusion to match the goal; its remaining premises
become subgoals.

The modification is discarded after the tactic call. The argument-free
`[selim]` theorem attribute registers the same classification persistently.
The plain `[elim]` attribute and `Elim` marker instead classify a rule as
unsafe.

### Failure

Constructing `SElim th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` has no suitable major premise or cannot be
converted to elimination-rule form.

### Example

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [clasetLib.SElim my_elim_rule]
```

The marked `my_elim_rule` is available only during this call.

